* Sense-margin bench: the committed efuse_sense subcircuit (design/efuse_otp_array.spice,
* extracted by run.sh together with efuse_comp) against a resistor standing in for the
* selected fuse. Circuit body for `klt sim` (no .control/.end). run.sh substitutes
* /home/ubuntu/.ciel/ciel/gf180mcu/versions/f6eeac7dad085ffcc829ccfd721f7b4ce39edcf7/gf180mcuD/libs.tech/ngspice/design.ngspice, 140 and @RREF@ and appends the two extracted subcircuits.
.include /home/ubuntu/.ciel/ciel/gf180mcu/versions/f6eeac7dad085ffcc829ccfd721f7b4ce39edcf7/gf180mcuD/libs.tech/ngspice/design.ngspice

* ASSUMPTION (A4/A5, no documented source beyond the 200 / 900 ohm points): the selected
* fuse is a plain resistor of the stated value. "open" is 1 Gohm.
.param rfuse=140
* Reference: efuse_sense carries Rref = 400 ohm (A6, decision 0003). The negative
* control rewrites that one line to @RREF@ ohm in the deck copy; the committed netlist
* is not touched.

* Sense/logic supply; klt sim alters source Vdd33 per corner (2.97 / 3.30 / 3.63 V).

Vdd33 vdd33 0 DC 3.3
* ASSUMPTION: program supply held at 5.0 V (A1 nominal). It only gates the 6 V select
* devices in the fuse and reference legs; the decision-0005 program-supply axis belongs
* to the program-path bench, not the sense margin.
Vvprog vprog 0 DC 5.0

* sense_en held asserted for the whole run.
Rsen sense_en vdd33 1
* One clock edge: clk low (comparator in reset, bias settling) until 15 ns, then high
* (evaluate). Amplitude tracks the corner's vdd33.
Bclk clk 0 V = v(vdd33) * min(max((time - 15n) / 200p, 0), 1)

* Device under test.
Xsa sbl sense_en clk sense_out vdd33 vprog 0 efuse_sense

* ASSUMPTION: fuse leg = fuse + the same series switch and select device the reference
* leg carries inside efuse_sense (Msw 4u / Msel 60u, nfet_06v0), so the bench isolates
* the resistor comparison. Bitline capacitance and column-mux leakage are not modelled.
Rf sbl fn {rfuse}
Xfsw fn sense_en fn2 0 nfet_06v0 L=0.7u W=4u nf=1
Xfsel fn2 vprog 0 0 nfet_06v0 L=0.7u W=60u nf=1

